1
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,920
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS.

2
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:44,440
Put it down.

3
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:46,000
Slow down.

4
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:49,200
Why are you sneaking around like that?

5
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:51,040
Take a look.

6
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:52,680
CINDY

7
00:01:52,760 --> 00:01:55,840
<i>One of my inside contacts</i>
<i>at Bolo Culture just tipped me off.</i>

8
00:01:55,920 --> 00:01:59,320
<i>She said she saw Lin Long getting</i>
<i>into Mr. Shen's car after work last night,</i>

9
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:00,800
<i>and they were all over each other.</i>

10
00:02:00,880 --> 00:02:02,760
<i>Those two have been acting weird lately.</i>

11
00:02:02,840 --> 00:02:04,640
<i>Ask her what's going on.</i>

12
00:02:04,720 --> 00:02:06,680
<i>Final delivery is coming up.</i>

13
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:10,240
<i>I don't want any drama</i>
<i>like with the Celestial project.</i>

14
00:02:10,759 --> 00:02:11,800
Is that true?

15
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:14,520
I just didn't drive that day.

16
00:02:14,600 --> 00:02:16,080
Mr. Shen gave me a ride.

17
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:17,120
Is it really that big a deal?

18
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:18,920
Cindy loves to make stuff up about me.

19
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:19,960
It's not the first time.

20
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,400
Seriously,

21
00:02:22,480 --> 00:02:23,800
I'm telling you, I've known you for years.

22
00:02:23,880 --> 00:02:26,440
You can't fool me.
Your face just now gave it away.

23
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:28,720
Did it?

24
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:29,840
Wait, no way.

25
00:02:29,920 --> 00:02:35,400
How could you make such a rookie mistake
and get tangled up with a client?

26
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:37,680
Don't tell me your divorce
messed you up so bad

27
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:39,320
your head's not on straight?

28
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:42,000
Listen, you need to pump the brakes.

29
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,960
Don't worry. No brakes needed.

30
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:45,360
Because nothing ever started.

31
00:02:45,440 --> 00:02:46,480
Really?

32
00:02:47,760 --> 00:02:48,840
That's good.

33
00:02:48,920 --> 00:02:51,840
I thought you weren't thinking straight
and would fall for it.

34
00:02:51,920 --> 00:02:55,000
With your situation right now,
how could Shen ever genuinely like you?

35
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:57,160
He's definitely just got a whim
and wants a taste of…

36
00:02:57,880 --> 00:02:59,880
A taste of something new. I get it.

37
00:03:00,600 --> 00:03:01,760
Excuse me.

38
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:05,880
Why would a unicorn startup founder
fall for someone like me,

39
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:07,280
a divorced woman?

40
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:11,880
So when I noticed
he might be even slightly into me,

41
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:14,160
I shut it down immediately.

42
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:17,560
I just asked him straight up. I asked him,

43
00:03:17,640 --> 00:03:18,840
"Do you have feelings for me?"

44
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:21,760
And sure enough,
he chickened out and backed off.

45
00:03:22,480 --> 00:03:24,760
Then why did you get
in his car last night?

46
00:03:26,320 --> 00:03:27,200
Because…

47
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:30,360
Because I'm a normal human being.

48
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:31,800
I think after clearing things up,

49
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:35,120
I have every right
to accept normal kindness from a guy.

50
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,840
And what era are we living in anyway?

51
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:41,560
I can't just feel inferior
to everyone else because I'm divorced.

52
00:03:41,640 --> 00:03:43,600
That's not what I meant.

53
00:03:43,680 --> 00:03:45,480
I know.

54
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,080
But I have to say,

55
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:52,440
when a guy who's got it all together

56
00:03:52,520 --> 00:03:55,120
wants to get close to you
and care for you,

57
00:03:55,200 --> 00:03:56,200
it's actually kind of nice.

58
00:03:57,720 --> 00:03:59,280
So that night,

59
00:03:59,360 --> 00:04:01,560
when he insisted on taking me
to get some trendy ice cream,

60
00:04:02,160 --> 00:04:03,160
I said yes.

61
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:05,440
But in the car, I was torn.

62
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:08,640
Part of me hated myself
for having no principles,

63
00:04:08,720 --> 00:04:10,760
but the rest of me was glad

64
00:04:10,840 --> 00:04:13,640
I still had it going on enough
to make a man fall for me.

65
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:18,920
I'm just so indecisive, hesitant…

66
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:19,920
And a total hypocrite.

67
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,200
But even now,
I don't think I did anything wrong.

68
00:04:24,840 --> 00:04:25,760
Hey you.

69
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:27,520
You didn't let him

70
00:04:28,760 --> 00:04:30,160
into your place last night, did you?

71
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:36,840
Come in.

72
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:01,360
Can I not answer that?

73
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,040
Of course.

74
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:12,840
MEETING ROOM

75
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:23,920
Let's talk when we get back.

76
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:32,240
Is it about Mr. Zheng?

77
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:36,640
Peng Yuan was fired and handed over
to economic crime investigators.

78
00:05:37,160 --> 00:05:38,640
Ma Ke is off the hook.

79
00:05:38,720 --> 00:05:40,240
His voluntary resignation is accepted.

80
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:42,680
Yang Rui will stay on with a new team.

81
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:46,240
The project will fully resume next week.

82
00:05:47,640 --> 00:05:48,600
We keep moving forward.

83
00:06:03,280 --> 00:06:05,600
I did my part today.

84
00:06:06,480 --> 00:06:08,360
Then keep it up

85
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:10,640
and go buy some milk tea
for everyone to celebrate.

86
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:11,680
Mango?

87
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:12,800
Medium matcha.

88
00:06:12,880 --> 00:06:14,320
Light ice, light sugar, no foam topping.

89
00:06:15,080 --> 00:06:16,560
Then I want choco…

90
00:06:19,760 --> 00:06:21,600
Never mind. I'm good.

91
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:36,320
I've known Richard for so long.

92
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,240
Looks like he's finally met the one.

93
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:01,720
HUANGHE BUSINESS SCHOOL EMBA
STRATEGIC MANAGEMENT

94
00:07:01,800 --> 00:07:02,800
RISKS, OPPORTUNITIES, AND STRATEGIC
RESPONSES IN DIGITAL COLLECTIBLES MARKET

95
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:04,000
SPEAKER: YE XINZHI, GUEST PROFESSOR

96
00:07:04,080 --> 00:07:04,920
The digital finance market

97
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,240
is like a blue ocean
full of hope and challenges.

98
00:07:07,760 --> 00:07:10,080
But opportunity and risk go hand in hand.

99
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:11,400
The domestic crypto market

100
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:12,680
has been through multiple rounds
of strict regulation

101
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:14,120
and is relatively stable now.

102
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:18,200
But the blockchain finance tied to it
is running wild in new forms.

103
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,680
Mr. Ye, what do you think
of digital collectibles?

104
00:07:20,760 --> 00:07:22,440
They're blowing up lately.

105
00:07:26,080 --> 00:07:27,920
That's a great question.

106
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:31,280
Digital collectibles have
massively expanded the art market.

107
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:32,440
Compared to traditional collectibles,

108
00:07:32,520 --> 00:07:34,320
they have better liquidity
and transparency,

109
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:38,520
which draws a ton
of eager investor attention.

110
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:40,360
I bought a few digital collectibles
to get in on the hype,

111
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:43,360
but I've noticed
a lot of people into digital collectibles

112
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:45,480
can't really explain
the business logic behind them.

113
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:49,080
Most just see them
as an alternative to crypto,

114
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:51,000
hoping to get rich overnight.

115
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:54,160
Especially with housing prices dropping
and the stock market weak lately,

116
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:56,400
lots of regular people
jumped on the bandwagon.

117
00:07:56,480 --> 00:07:57,360
But the overhyping

118
00:07:57,440 --> 00:08:00,360
has pushed the risk
to a pretty alarming level.

119
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:05,280
Everyone, you're the ones
shaping the market policy.

120
00:08:05,880 --> 00:08:08,960
And steady industry growth
needs everyone's input.

121
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:11,880
Since we're on the topic
of digital collectibles today,

122
00:08:11,960 --> 00:08:13,240
I'll just assign a paper.

123
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:15,960
Research on the Operational Models
and Risk Prevention

124
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:17,280
of Domestic Digital Collectibles.

125
00:08:17,880 --> 00:08:19,360
Work in groups.

126
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:20,960
We'll discuss it in the next class.

127
00:08:21,040 --> 00:08:22,840
That's it for today. Class is over.

128
00:08:33,440 --> 00:08:36,559
- Mr. Ye, can we add each other on WeChat?
- Sure.

129
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:38,919
Let me scan yours.

130
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,960
What you talked about today
was so helpful to us.

131
00:08:42,039 --> 00:08:43,880
Hope we can hear
more from you in the future.

132
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:45,440
- Thank you.
- Thanks so much.

133
00:08:50,560 --> 00:08:52,080
Hello there, Mr. Ye.

134
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:53,880
Nice try.

135
00:08:53,960 --> 00:08:56,320
Miss Xu, you weren't
paying attention in class,

136
00:08:56,400 --> 00:08:57,960
sipping milk tea
and goofing off down there.

137
00:08:58,040 --> 00:08:59,720
I'm going to have to give you
a serious lecture.

138
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:03,600
Guess I'll have to bribe you then,

139
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:05,280
so you won't fail me on the final.

140
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:08,040
That's more like it.

141
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:19,840
What you just said was spot on.

142
00:09:20,360 --> 00:09:22,080
You assigned the paper so naturally.

143
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:24,520
Yuanzhou is such a hot topic right now.

144
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:25,720
Everyone will definitely use it

145
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,560
as a case study
and dig deep into its problems.

146
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:31,960
But is that really efficient?

147
00:09:33,440 --> 00:09:36,840
The person I just added on WeChat
is from the Internet Finance Association.

148
00:09:37,520 --> 00:09:38,560
What do you think?

149
00:09:44,480 --> 00:09:45,960
SHEN JIN, BOLO CULTURE

150
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:56,720
- What are you doing?
- I called you 124 times.

151
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:58,760
- Why didn't you pick up?
- Didn't hear it.

152
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:00,760
Then why did you block me on WeChat?

153
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:02,720
I added you on WeCom, sir.

154
00:10:02,800 --> 00:10:06,400
It's easier for colleagues
to reach you there going forward.

155
00:10:07,080 --> 00:10:08,320
- What did you just call me?
- Sir.

156
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:11,000
So we're being all formal now?

157
00:10:11,760 --> 00:10:13,680
Mr. Shen, we're just business partners.

158
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:18,720
Lin Long, you're kicking me
to the curb now?

159
00:10:18,800 --> 00:10:19,720
Use me and toss me aside?

160
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:21,040
You're playing me for a fool?

161
00:10:21,120 --> 00:10:22,240
No, Mr. Shen--

162
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:25,000
Who was it that night,
all sweet and tender, asking…

163
00:10:25,080 --> 00:10:27,240
asking if her old ticket
could still get her--

164
00:10:27,320 --> 00:10:28,760
Okay, stop. Nothing happened that night…

165
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:29,960
- No, hold on…
- Nothing happened that night…

166
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:31,080
- Let's get this straight.
- I completely forgot.

167
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:32,000
Lin!

168
00:10:34,640 --> 00:10:35,960
Are you two okay?

169
00:10:36,560 --> 00:10:37,400
We're fine.

170
00:10:37,480 --> 00:10:40,360
Mr. Shen, let's just talk on WeCom
if we need anything.

171
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:41,480
I'm leaving. Bye.

172
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:42,640
- Bye.
- Bye.

173
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:08,360
- I'm really sorry. I…
- You're bleeding.

174
00:12:08,440 --> 00:12:10,680
You're pregnant.
How could you drive so carelessly?

175
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:12,320
Is the baby okay?

176
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:15,480
Look at you. You're thin as a rail.

177
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:19,040
If you haven't fully recovered,
don't rush back to work.

178
00:12:19,120 --> 00:12:20,000
Why push yourself?

179
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:22,080
Xu Chi brought this to me before.

180
00:12:22,160 --> 00:12:23,760
She said you specifically asked for it,

181
00:12:23,840 --> 00:12:24,640
and she passed along that message.

182
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:27,640
"A rebirth through hardship
and better days ahead."

183
00:12:27,720 --> 00:12:29,440
I've had my share of hardship.

184
00:12:29,520 --> 00:12:32,240
Now it's time to earn those better days
with my own two hands.

185
00:12:33,880 --> 00:12:35,000
Want to watch this one?

186
00:12:36,800 --> 00:12:38,080
Looks boring.

187
00:12:38,160 --> 00:12:39,120
They say it's good.

188
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:41,000
Let's go.

189
00:12:41,520 --> 00:12:43,720
I'm serious. Want to give it a shot?

190
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:16,920
Long.

191
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:21,280
How have you been?

192
00:13:29,240 --> 00:13:30,360
You're back at work?

193
00:13:30,880 --> 00:13:31,720
Why didn't you take more time off?

194
00:13:32,840 --> 00:13:33,680
None of your business.

195
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:36,080
Long, listen to me.

196
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:37,600
- I've actually always wanted to tell you…
- Let go of me.

197
00:13:37,680 --> 00:13:38,640
- I don't want to hear it.
- Zhiwen.

198
00:13:40,400 --> 00:13:41,320
Who is she?

199
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:45,920
Just a friend. Just ran into each other.

200
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:47,320
Are you playing me for a fool?

201
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:49,040
Isn't she your ex-wife?

202
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:49,960
What's the deal with you two?

203
00:13:50,040 --> 00:13:52,480
You're divorced and still flirting?

204
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:55,440
He's right. He's playing you for a fool.

205
00:13:56,520 --> 00:13:57,720
Who are you calling a fool?

206
00:13:57,800 --> 00:13:59,400
You're the shameless one
throwing yourself at my boyfriend!

207
00:13:59,480 --> 00:14:01,400
- Don't you know he has a girlfriend now?
- Lin Long!

208
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:02,320
I knew you'd be here.

209
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:05,200
- Give it here.
- Are these two your friends?

210
00:14:05,280 --> 00:14:06,400
Give it here.

211
00:14:06,480 --> 00:14:07,280
Car keys.

212
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:13,640
I didn't want to say this

213
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:17,480
because I think two women fighting
over a guy is just pathetic.

214
00:14:18,280 --> 00:14:20,440
But to settle this once and for all,
I'll just tell you straight.

215
00:14:20,520 --> 00:14:22,840
This guy you're treating like a prize?

216
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:24,000
I dumped him a long time ago.

217
00:14:24,080 --> 00:14:25,360
And him?

218
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:28,000
He chased me around in fancy cars,
and I still wasn't interested.

219
00:14:28,080 --> 00:14:30,960
A divorced guy making less than me,
destined to be laid off by 40,

220
00:14:31,040 --> 00:14:33,440
doing nothing but playing
video games all day?

221
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:35,040
You're welcome to him.

222
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:42,520
She doesn't really get it.

223
00:14:43,880 --> 00:14:44,800
This car's actually nothing special.

224
00:14:44,880 --> 00:14:46,600
I've got a few more at home.

225
00:14:54,680 --> 00:14:55,840
Lin Long.

226
00:14:57,160 --> 00:14:59,320
- Stop following me.
- I know.

227
00:14:59,840 --> 00:15:03,640
I just wanted to say
you were really badass back there.

228
00:15:04,280 --> 00:15:05,640
Badass. Not "bad".

229
00:15:05,720 --> 00:15:06,720
I'm not insulting you.

230
00:15:07,240 --> 00:15:08,480
That day outside the bathroom,

231
00:15:08,560 --> 00:15:10,440
you went off on me just like that too.

232
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:11,880
And I just thought…

233
00:15:15,440 --> 00:15:17,440
Do you just like getting kicked around?

234
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:19,640
Maybe I do.

235
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:22,880
Shen Jin. Open your eyes and look at me.

236
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:26,040
I'm just a divorced woman
trying to prove she's still got it.

237
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:28,000
Shallow, vain, and a total coward.

238
00:15:28,520 --> 00:15:31,680
I do want to thank you
for keeping me company when I was lonely.

239
00:15:31,760 --> 00:15:33,200
And sorry about just now.

240
00:15:33,280 --> 00:15:34,600
I had to use you to put on a front,

241
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:36,840
so I could keep
what little dignity I have left

242
00:15:36,920 --> 00:15:38,080
in front of my ex-husband.

243
00:15:39,400 --> 00:15:41,200
And didn't you say
you felt nothing for me?

244
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:43,160
So why are you clinging to me like this?

245
00:15:43,680 --> 00:15:44,760
Just because you can't stand losing?

246
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:50,080
Or is it because a guy with your money
has never been dumped like this before?

247
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:52,040
So, should I pay you
for emotional damages then?

248
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:57,240
Lin Long,

249
00:15:58,160 --> 00:16:00,360
am I really that terrible?

250
00:16:00,440 --> 00:16:02,880
So terrible that you have to run away
every time you see me?

251
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,600
And are you really that insecure?

252
00:16:05,680 --> 00:16:09,040
All you did was get a divorce
and hook up with a guy.

253
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:12,760
How does that turn into being
a coward, insecure, and shallow?

254
00:16:13,880 --> 00:16:15,160
If you were really like that,

255
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:17,480
I wouldn't have been chasing you this long
with zero shame.

256
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:19,960
I know.

257
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:22,120
You've been avoiding me

258
00:16:22,640 --> 00:16:27,560
because I chickened out
when you asked if I had feelings for you.

259
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:30,120
Back then, I told you
it was just sympathy.

260
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:34,880
But love isn't some high-stakes exam.

261
00:16:35,400 --> 00:16:37,160
Can't I change my answer
if I got it wrong?

262
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:41,240
I admit I didn't mean
what I said that day.

263
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:44,600
Later, I figured it out.
I really regret it.

264
00:16:46,080 --> 00:16:49,320
I'm not some young girl
who falls for fairy tales anymore.

265
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:53,400
What you feel for me now
is just admiration and curiosity.

266
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:55,640
Maybe mixed with a little
wounded pride and the need to win.

267
00:16:55,720 --> 00:16:56,960
If I said yes,

268
00:16:57,040 --> 00:16:58,600
you'd get bored of me
in less than a month.

269
00:16:59,440 --> 00:17:00,520
And me?

270
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:02,720
I'd be really disappointed and hurt.

271
00:17:02,800 --> 00:17:06,160
Maybe I'd fall back
into that crazy mess I used to be.

272
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:07,920
Like how I was when you first met me.

273
00:17:08,800 --> 00:17:10,800
Remember when I rear-ended your car?

274
00:17:10,880 --> 00:17:13,359
There wasn't an ounce
of admiration in your eyes.

275
00:17:15,520 --> 00:17:17,760
So if you think I'm badass now,

276
00:17:17,839 --> 00:17:20,760
please just let me hold
onto this fragile pride of mine. Okay?

277
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:23,200
Because after the divorce,

278
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:26,000
I don't have much pride left.

279
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:38,840
Thank you.

280
00:18:04,280 --> 00:18:05,120
What are you doing here?

281
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:16,520
Aren't you supposed
to be heading to the airport?

282
00:18:17,600 --> 00:18:19,640
Driving my girlfriend to work
is more important than a business trip.

283
00:18:19,720 --> 00:18:20,600
Get in.

284
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:29,960
Actually, I just woke up to a notification
that my flight got delayed.

285
00:18:30,040 --> 00:18:33,160
Plus, I have some great news for you,

286
00:18:33,240 --> 00:18:34,080
so I came over.

287
00:18:34,160 --> 00:18:36,640
What great news?

288
00:18:36,720 --> 00:18:38,120
Give me your bank account number.

289
00:18:38,720 --> 00:18:39,760
Morse's bonus came through.

290
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:40,880
One million.

291
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:42,840
If it's not enough for a down payment,

292
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:44,560
I can chip in.

293
00:18:45,880 --> 00:18:46,760
It's enough.

294
00:18:47,280 --> 00:18:49,200
With what I've saved,
it's definitely enough.

295
00:18:49,280 --> 00:18:50,760
And apartment prices
have been dropping lately.

296
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:51,680
This is more than enough!

297
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:57,480
This is… This is such great news.

298
00:18:58,680 --> 00:19:01,120
Xinzhi, thank you so much.

299
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:04,800
Don't just say it. Show me.

300
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:07,480
You're still driving.

301
00:19:22,760 --> 00:19:24,320
Message me when you land.

302
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:26,000
- Bye.
- Bye.

303
00:19:33,280 --> 00:19:34,240
Morning.

304
00:19:36,440 --> 00:19:37,960
Morning. You're here for work too.

305
00:19:40,280 --> 00:19:42,240
Is that him? Your new boyfriend?

306
00:19:46,720 --> 00:19:47,800
Nice car.

307
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:49,640
No wonder you broke up with me.

308
00:19:49,720 --> 00:19:52,040
We broke up because we weren't compatible,

309
00:19:52,120 --> 00:19:53,520
not because he drives a fancy car.

310
00:19:56,440 --> 00:19:57,560
I'm sorry.

311
00:20:00,200 --> 00:20:01,120
And I owe you a thank-you.

312
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,640
If it weren't for you,

313
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:05,040
I wouldn't have kept this job.

314
00:20:06,280 --> 00:20:07,120
It's fine.

315
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:10,320
Can we still be friends?

316
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:17,320
I've already repaid the favor
from when you helped me

317
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:18,800
during the team-building.

318
00:20:19,520 --> 00:20:20,440
Let's just be colleagues from now on.

319
00:20:39,800 --> 00:20:41,320
What are you doing here?

320
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:42,800
They had me swap project teams
with Yang Rui.

321
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:44,880
Then go sit over there.

322
00:20:47,200 --> 00:20:48,320
Why are you still keeping your distance?

323
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:50,200
Everyone who needs to know
already knows anyway.

324
00:21:07,760 --> 00:21:10,640
The Celestial project is back on track.

325
00:21:10,720 --> 00:21:14,280
Today's meeting is mainly
about restructuring the project team.

326
00:21:15,080 --> 00:21:17,000
Zhou Sen, Tianna, Du Qian.

327
00:21:17,080 --> 00:21:19,400
You'll still be in charge
of your original teams.

328
00:21:19,920 --> 00:21:20,800
Okay.

329
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:24,640
Xu Chi, IT was at the heart
of the last mess,

330
00:21:24,720 --> 00:21:26,920
but I want you
to take the lead on it this time.

331
00:21:27,640 --> 00:21:29,520
Li Yue has experience in this area.

332
00:21:29,600 --> 00:21:31,720
- He'll back you up.
- Okay.

333
00:21:33,160 --> 00:21:34,960
As for the new project manager,

334
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:36,720
the higher-ups haven't decided yet.

335
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:39,120
I mean, we're already
more than halfway through this project.

336
00:21:39,200 --> 00:21:42,400
Bringing in a new consultant now
wouldn't be ideal.

337
00:21:42,480 --> 00:21:43,640
So Mr. Pi wants to pick

338
00:21:43,720 --> 00:21:47,120
one of the team leads
to fill in as acting manager.

339
00:21:47,200 --> 00:21:48,840
I'd like to hear what everyone thinks.

340
00:21:50,520 --> 00:21:51,360
Who do you think it'll be?

341
00:21:51,440 --> 00:21:53,840
You think I've got a shot?

342
00:21:54,760 --> 00:21:56,320
But we're just analysts.

343
00:21:56,400 --> 00:21:59,080
So what? Can't we aim higher?

344
00:22:00,120 --> 00:22:01,360
I'd like to nominate Tianna.

345
00:22:01,440 --> 00:22:02,560
Ever since Ma Ke's suspension,

346
00:22:02,640 --> 00:22:05,640
she's been coordinating
and running the entire project.

347
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:06,760
Seconded.

348
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:10,160
Wow.

349
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:14,440
Now I finally get what it means
to be the obvious choice.

350
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:18,480
Okay. Then let's congratulate Tianna

351
00:22:19,080 --> 00:22:21,520
on becoming Maxmise's
youngest project manager.

352
00:22:23,520 --> 00:22:24,880
Thank you, everyone.

353
00:22:30,840 --> 00:22:32,720
You all know I hate talking fluff,

354
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:34,400
though that sentence itself was fluff.

355
00:22:34,480 --> 00:22:37,760
So now let me walk you through
my plan and progress

356
00:22:37,840 --> 00:22:39,520
since the project kicked off.

357
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:53,160
Jealous?

358
00:22:57,120 --> 00:22:58,320
I'm just…

359
00:23:00,040 --> 00:23:01,560
I just

360
00:23:02,360 --> 00:23:03,480
wasn't ready for this.

361
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:08,360
Honestly, when we both got promoted
to SBA around the same time,

362
00:23:08,440 --> 00:23:09,600
I was fine with it.

363
00:23:09,680 --> 00:23:14,400
But then she just shot past me
and became a project manager.

364
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:17,440
- I just feel a little…
- I get it.

365
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:21,560
Back when you took
the Bolo Culture project from me,

366
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:22,480
I felt the same way.

367
00:23:22,560 --> 00:23:25,720
- Lin…
- I'm just kidding.

368
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:29,680
Actually, this kind of thing happens
all the time at the company.

369
00:23:29,760 --> 00:23:31,280
Just like Lu Le and me.

370
00:23:31,360 --> 00:23:34,880
We're friends, but we're also rivals.

371
00:23:34,960 --> 00:23:36,000
So don't worry about it.

372
00:23:36,080 --> 00:23:37,720
After a few more times,
you'll get used to it.

373
00:23:38,600 --> 00:23:39,640
I know.

374
00:23:39,720 --> 00:23:41,760
It's not that I'm scared
to compete with her.

375
00:23:41,840 --> 00:23:43,800
When we were doing
the draft for Celestial,

376
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:45,200
we went head-to-head.

377
00:23:45,960 --> 00:23:46,880
I just…

378
00:23:48,560 --> 00:23:51,360
And Tianna didn't tell me anything.

379
00:23:51,440 --> 00:23:53,280
I didn't even know she took over
the whole Celestial project

380
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:55,000
while I was suspended.

381
00:23:57,560 --> 00:24:00,720
When you were suspended,
you went to help Morse pull off a deal.

382
00:24:00,800 --> 00:24:01,880
You didn't tell Tianna
about that beforehand, did you?

383
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:06,400
There's no such thing
as absolute fairness in the workplace.

384
00:24:06,480 --> 00:24:08,600
While you're grinding,
other people aren't just sitting around.

385
00:24:09,600 --> 00:24:11,960
Back when Celestial and Maxmise
were at each other's throats,

386
00:24:12,040 --> 00:24:14,400
everyone thought the project was done for.

387
00:24:14,480 --> 00:24:15,840
But Tianna was the only one
who didn't give up.

388
00:24:15,920 --> 00:24:18,840
She went to Mr. Pi and fought
to keep the project from being shut down.

389
00:24:18,920 --> 00:24:22,440
She coordinated with colleagues
to go through the investigation,

390
00:24:22,520 --> 00:24:23,880
while keeping the project moving.

391
00:24:24,760 --> 00:24:27,800
So without her drive and effort,

392
00:24:27,880 --> 00:24:30,920
do you really think Celestial would've
decided to restart the whole project

393
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:32,960
the second they saw
your evidence clearing Ma Ke?

394
00:24:40,920 --> 00:24:41,840
I get it.

395
00:24:42,880 --> 00:24:47,760
I really have no right
to be jealous of her.

396
00:24:50,400 --> 00:24:51,280
Thanks for setting me straight.

397
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:54,880
Call it payback.

398
00:24:54,960 --> 00:24:58,160
After all, I was a pretty lousy mentor.

399
00:24:58,240 --> 00:24:59,720
I never really gave you any real guidance.

400
00:25:02,560 --> 00:25:05,720
But now I think you're actually grounded.

401
00:25:05,800 --> 00:25:09,120
Like a girl who hasn't been
out of school for long.

402
00:25:09,200 --> 00:25:13,800
Not like one of those prodigy girls
you only see in books or TV shows.

403
00:25:18,960 --> 00:25:20,080
Is this more like it?

404
00:25:23,800 --> 00:25:24,920
Let me check a message.

405
00:25:33,520 --> 00:25:35,480
That's the amulet
Mr. Shen gave you, right?

406
00:25:35,560 --> 00:25:36,600
You're still wearing it.

407
00:25:39,560 --> 00:25:40,400
No idea if it even works.

408
00:25:40,480 --> 00:25:42,280
I use it as a phone charm.

409
00:25:42,360 --> 00:25:43,200
Just got used to it.

410
00:26:44,480 --> 00:26:46,200
I zoned out.

411
00:26:46,720 --> 00:26:48,480
I just suddenly thought

412
00:26:48,560 --> 00:26:50,520
of something I discussed
in a call with Celestial.

413
00:26:53,920 --> 00:26:54,800
Don't push yourself so hard.

414
00:26:56,000 --> 00:26:57,600
I've already been
on two business trips this week.

415
00:26:57,680 --> 00:27:00,280
We only get two hours together today,

416
00:27:00,360 --> 00:27:01,440
and you're still working so hard.

417
00:27:01,520 --> 00:27:02,800
You're practically getting dark circles.

418
00:27:04,720 --> 00:27:05,800
Do I have them?

419
00:27:06,320 --> 00:27:07,400
Where?

420
00:27:07,480 --> 00:27:09,200
Just kidding.

421
00:27:11,160 --> 00:27:13,000
Back when you were my protege,

422
00:27:13,080 --> 00:27:15,200
I could only tell you to take it easy
when I saw you grinding like this.

423
00:27:16,000 --> 00:27:17,880
But now, as your boyfriend,

424
00:27:17,960 --> 00:27:20,560
I have to seriously tell you
to stop pushing so hard.

425
00:27:21,080 --> 00:27:23,320
Don't treat yourself like a work machine.

426
00:27:24,000 --> 00:27:26,480
Consulting is a marathon of output.

427
00:27:26,560 --> 00:27:28,120
If you keep pulling
all-nighters like this,

428
00:27:28,200 --> 00:27:30,200
you'll burn yourself out sooner or later.

429
00:27:45,120 --> 00:27:47,280
What's wrong? Tired of me nagging?

430
00:27:49,640 --> 00:27:52,640
I just want your work to be easier.

431
00:27:54,160 --> 00:27:57,600
But we both prefer seeing
each other strive to do better, right?

432
00:28:00,360 --> 00:28:01,200
Okay, okay.

433
00:28:01,720 --> 00:28:03,760
Whatever the lady says goes.

434
00:28:05,960 --> 00:28:07,080
I think so too.

435
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:09,360
- Eat up.
- Eat up.

436
00:28:22,760 --> 00:28:23,840
Honestly,

437
00:28:24,840 --> 00:28:26,280
I just want to push a little harder.

438
00:28:26,360 --> 00:28:28,160
I don't want to be outdone by Tianna.

439
00:28:30,920 --> 00:28:31,760
I get it.

440
00:28:32,480 --> 00:28:34,160
But don't forget

441
00:28:34,240 --> 00:28:36,000
why you got into this industry
in the first place.

442
00:28:37,200 --> 00:28:39,840
Don't let specific issues
get you completely bogged down.

443
00:28:40,640 --> 00:28:42,200
Of course I haven't forgotten.

444
00:28:42,280 --> 00:28:45,080
I want to be a top consultant like you,

445
00:28:45,160 --> 00:28:46,080
make partner,

446
00:28:46,160 --> 00:28:48,680
have my own office,
and buy back my mom's old apartment.

447
00:28:50,480 --> 00:28:51,320
Apartment.

448
00:28:53,200 --> 00:28:55,480
I told the agent this morning
that I had the money ready.

449
00:28:56,000 --> 00:28:58,120
I've been so busy all day
that I forgot to ask him for an update.

450
00:28:58,200 --> 00:28:59,560
Where's my phone?

451
00:29:00,520 --> 00:29:01,360
Right here.

452
00:29:02,080 --> 00:29:03,160
Any updates?

453
00:29:04,240 --> 00:29:05,640
The agent said apartment prices
dropped again.

454
00:29:05,720 --> 00:29:07,920
The guy who signed online before
changed his mind and backed out.

455
00:29:08,680 --> 00:29:10,400
Then the landlord said

456
00:29:10,480 --> 00:29:13,080
if I could pay the same price,
he'd sell it to me.

457
00:29:13,160 --> 00:29:14,160
That's great news.

458
00:29:15,640 --> 00:29:17,000
Hey, Zhu. This is Xu Chi.

459
00:29:17,080 --> 00:29:19,080
How did it go?
When did the landlord say we could sign?

460
00:29:22,720 --> 00:29:24,440
What? How could he just
change his mind like that?

461
00:29:24,520 --> 00:29:25,520
What happened?

462
00:29:26,720 --> 00:29:27,560
The landlord backed out.

463
00:29:27,640 --> 00:29:29,600
He said I need to pay in full
to close the deal.

464
00:29:31,480 --> 00:29:32,360
Don't panic just yet.

465
00:29:32,440 --> 00:29:34,360
Let's head over right now
and talk to him in person.

466
00:29:36,400 --> 00:29:39,160
Xu, we go way back.
How could I pull anything on you?

467
00:29:39,240 --> 00:29:40,720
The landlord already agreed.

468
00:29:40,800 --> 00:29:42,400
He even went to the transaction center.

469
00:29:42,480 --> 00:29:44,880
But the paperwork to cancel the signing
and get the tax refund is a hassle.

470
00:29:44,960 --> 00:29:46,760
He got annoyed
and didn't want to deal with it.

471
00:29:47,480 --> 00:29:49,880
He said if he sold it to you,
he'd have to make trips again,

472
00:29:49,960 --> 00:29:52,800
and waiting for your loan approval
would take months.

473
00:29:52,880 --> 00:29:56,760
So either you pay in full
or he's not canceling the signing.

474
00:29:56,840 --> 00:29:58,120
Come on.

475
00:29:58,200 --> 00:30:00,120
Banks approve mortgages really fast now.

476
00:30:00,200 --> 00:30:01,840
And I know people there.
I definitely won't drag it out.

477
00:30:02,760 --> 00:30:03,800
How about this?

478
00:30:05,200 --> 00:30:07,480
Can you help me contact him
so I can talk to him in person?

479
00:30:07,560 --> 00:30:09,680
But it's 11 p.m. now.

480
00:30:09,760 --> 00:30:10,920
He's probably asleep.

481
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:14,320
Besides, the notes say
he's only available during the day.

482
00:30:15,120 --> 00:30:16,720
- Then… Then I…
- Easy now.

483
00:30:18,840 --> 00:30:20,640
The landlord really said
it has to be full payment, right?

484
00:30:20,720 --> 00:30:22,640
Yes… It's true. Why would I lie to you?

485
00:30:22,720 --> 00:30:26,200
Whether you pay in full or take a loan,
our commission is the same.

486
00:30:26,280 --> 00:30:28,440
The landlord wouldn't
let us see the place.

487
00:30:28,520 --> 00:30:30,200
Now he's about to sell it.

488
00:30:30,280 --> 00:30:31,320
Can you take us to see it?

489
00:30:32,960 --> 00:30:33,800
Alright.

490
00:30:44,840 --> 00:30:47,120
I'll step out and take a call.

491
00:30:55,320 --> 00:30:57,760
Remember which room
you stayed in as a kid?

492
00:31:00,320 --> 00:31:01,800
It should be this one.

493
00:31:09,080 --> 00:31:10,360
No, I think it was this one.

494
00:31:11,880 --> 00:31:12,920
You don't remember?

495
00:31:19,320 --> 00:31:21,400
This used to be my grandma's apartment.

496
00:31:22,200 --> 00:31:25,120
I only got to come and stay here
with my mom during the holidays.

497
00:31:26,840 --> 00:31:28,040
It's been so many years.

498
00:31:28,920 --> 00:31:31,360
This place looks nothing like I remember.

499
00:31:37,480 --> 00:31:38,440
All I remember

500
00:31:39,680 --> 00:31:43,400
is that my mom sold it for 80,000 yuan
to help my dad fund his business.

501
00:31:45,040 --> 00:31:47,800
Then my dad got a mistress.

502
00:31:48,320 --> 00:31:49,800
My mom divorced him.

503
00:31:51,080 --> 00:31:53,920
When my mom saw on the news that
apartment prices here had skyrocketed,

504
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:55,280
she regretted it so much.

505
00:31:57,720 --> 00:32:00,280
Before my mom passed,
she told me so many times.

506
00:32:01,720 --> 00:32:04,280
She said she really wanted to go back
to before she met my dad.

507
00:32:06,200 --> 00:32:07,600
Back to Beijing.

508
00:32:09,640 --> 00:32:10,800
Back to this apartment.

509
00:32:16,280 --> 00:32:17,840
But I was too young then.

510
00:32:18,920 --> 00:32:20,280
There was nothing I could do.

511
00:32:20,880 --> 00:32:24,480
Is this her wish or yours?

512
00:32:26,640 --> 00:32:27,840
Is there a difference?

513
00:32:30,800 --> 00:32:33,760
Anyway, every time I'm sad, I come here.

514
00:32:33,840 --> 00:32:38,240
Just looking at this little building
and that window full of flowers,

515
00:32:38,760 --> 00:32:40,200
it's like I go back in time.

516
00:32:40,840 --> 00:32:44,600
Back to when I was happiest.

517
00:32:53,960 --> 00:32:55,360
Then let's buy this place.

518
00:32:57,960 --> 00:32:59,360
I don't have that kind of money.

519
00:32:59,440 --> 00:33:00,720
You've got me.

520
00:33:04,240 --> 00:33:05,880
That's not what I meant.

521
00:33:05,960 --> 00:33:06,920
Sometimes,

522
00:33:07,560 --> 00:33:09,440
opportunity matters more than money.

523
00:33:09,520 --> 00:33:12,480
- But I can't just use your money.
- You already missed out once.

524
00:33:13,080 --> 00:33:14,400
You can't miss it again.

525
00:33:14,480 --> 00:33:16,520
If it really bothers you,

526
00:33:17,240 --> 00:33:18,720
we can sign a loan agreement.

527
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:24,840
Chi, give me a chance
to do what a boyfriend should do.

528
00:33:26,040 --> 00:33:26,880
Alright?

529
00:34:11,880 --> 00:34:12,800
Hey, ladies.

530
00:34:12,880 --> 00:34:14,639
Long time no see.

531
00:34:14,719 --> 00:34:15,639
Missed you guys so much.

532
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:23,360
Let me give you a quick update.

533
00:34:23,440 --> 00:34:25,800
Today I'm doing the preliminary delivery
with the Reinsurance Department.

534
00:34:27,120 --> 00:34:28,120
Let's talk about it
at the morning meeting.

535
00:34:28,199 --> 00:34:30,760
- Okay.
- Uh, I can't make the morning meeting.

536
00:34:30,840 --> 00:34:32,560
And I need to take some time off.

537
00:34:32,639 --> 00:34:35,760
At 8:40, I'm meeting Mr. Sun
to check the database.

538
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:37,400
And tomorrow, I'm going
on a business trip with him.

539
00:34:38,080 --> 00:34:40,120
We're hitting Celestial's data centers

540
00:34:40,199 --> 00:34:42,239
in Guangzhou, Shenzhen,
Chengdu, and Suzhou

541
00:34:42,320 --> 00:34:44,400
to do on-site training delivery.

542
00:34:44,480 --> 00:34:46,000
Probably won't be back until the weekend.

543
00:34:46,080 --> 00:34:47,600
That many places in such a short time?

544
00:34:47,679 --> 00:34:48,679
Can your body handle it?

545
00:34:49,280 --> 00:34:51,440
Okay, as long
as you've got it planned out.

546
00:34:51,520 --> 00:34:52,679
No need to send daily reports.

547
00:34:52,760 --> 00:34:53,920
Just give me a summary when you're back.

548
00:34:56,280 --> 00:34:57,120
IT Department's on the 17th floor.

549
00:34:57,200 --> 00:34:58,560
I'll take the high-zone elevator.

550
00:34:58,640 --> 00:34:59,840
Bye.

551
00:35:03,320 --> 00:35:05,080
My bad. My bad.

552
00:35:08,200 --> 00:35:11,960
She's grinding right now,
trying to pull ahead of me.

553
00:35:12,040 --> 00:35:13,080
Don't hold her back.

554
00:35:13,640 --> 00:35:14,600
No way.

555
00:35:14,680 --> 00:35:16,560
You've already been project manager
for some time.

556
00:35:16,640 --> 00:35:18,280
Even if she knocks it out of the park
with the IT Department,

557
00:35:18,360 --> 00:35:19,200
she still can't top you.

558
00:35:19,280 --> 00:35:21,680
Do you really think this hand-me-down
project manager spot

559
00:35:21,760 --> 00:35:22,640
is worth all that much?

560
00:35:22,720 --> 00:35:25,000
She and I are both gunning for a partner.

561
00:35:25,080 --> 00:35:27,280
You think we care
about some temporary title? No.

562
00:35:27,360 --> 00:35:29,520
What we care about is Mr. Pi and Sha Sha's

563
00:35:29,600 --> 00:35:32,440
overall evaluation
after this project wraps.

564
00:35:32,520 --> 00:35:34,880
That affects how far I can go at Maxmise.

565
00:35:35,480 --> 00:35:36,920
- Get it?
- Got it.

566
00:35:39,160 --> 00:35:41,080
Okay, I'm done talking to you.

567
00:35:41,680 --> 00:35:42,520
Have to go grind too.

568
00:35:45,440 --> 00:35:46,280
How about this?

569
00:35:46,360 --> 00:35:49,280
Let me grind with you at your place
these next few days?

570
00:35:52,440 --> 00:35:53,400
You wish.

571
00:36:02,680 --> 00:36:04,240
MOM

572
00:36:06,600 --> 00:36:08,320
I'll take the stairs.

573
00:36:12,560 --> 00:36:13,640
Hey, Mom.

574
00:36:14,560 --> 00:36:16,000
What's up? I'm at work.

575
00:36:18,600 --> 00:36:19,600
A blind date?

576
00:36:21,040 --> 00:36:21,960
I'm not going.

577
00:36:22,040 --> 00:36:23,000
You guys promised me

578
00:36:23,080 --> 00:36:25,800
you'd never pull this blind date
nonsense on me. I…

579
00:36:27,560 --> 00:36:28,400
Dad.

580
00:36:30,400 --> 00:36:32,880
Okay, I got it.

581
00:36:32,960 --> 00:36:33,960
I'll be there on time.

582
00:36:48,200 --> 00:36:49,400
BETTER HOME TOGETHER

583
00:37:05,080 --> 00:37:06,040
Tianna.

584
00:37:06,560 --> 00:37:09,160
Ms. Xue's son works in IT.

585
00:37:09,240 --> 00:37:12,040
I heard he's doing really well.

586
00:37:13,200 --> 00:37:14,680
Wow, that's impressive.

587
00:37:15,200 --> 00:37:17,640
So if my laptop breaks,
can he fix it for me?

588
00:37:17,720 --> 00:37:18,600
Don't be silly.

589
00:37:18,680 --> 00:37:20,720
His company is huge.

590
00:37:21,240 --> 00:37:23,480
Come on. Don't pull that long face.

591
00:37:23,560 --> 00:37:27,360
Your dad wanted you to come
and vet the guy for him.

592
00:37:27,440 --> 00:37:29,240
He recently got into some…

593
00:37:29,920 --> 00:37:30,960
What's it called again?

594
00:37:31,040 --> 00:37:32,720
It's a new business model, anyway.

595
00:37:33,360 --> 00:37:34,360
Perfect timing.

596
00:37:34,440 --> 00:37:36,920
Ms. Xue's son works in tech.

597
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:38,840
Don't overthink it.

598
00:37:38,920 --> 00:37:40,280
It's not a blind date.

599
00:37:40,360 --> 00:37:42,240
Just think of it as making a new friend.

600
00:37:43,200 --> 00:37:44,160
Have a nice chat.

601
00:37:45,520 --> 00:37:46,760
Right this way. It's this private room.

602
00:37:46,840 --> 00:37:48,080
Thank you. Hui!

603
00:37:49,280 --> 00:37:51,080
- Come on.
- You're already here.

604
00:37:51,680 --> 00:37:54,000
- Mrs. Xue is here.
- So sorry. We're late.

605
00:37:54,080 --> 00:37:55,800
- Son, come on.
- Quick.

606
00:37:55,880 --> 00:37:57,480
- Long time no see.
- Exactly.

607
00:37:57,560 --> 00:37:59,080
- And this is…?
- Tianna.

608
00:37:59,160 --> 00:38:00,400
Say hi.

609
00:38:00,480 --> 00:38:02,440
- Hi, Ms. Xue.
- Hello.

610
00:38:02,520 --> 00:38:03,600
So pretty.

611
00:38:04,120 --> 00:38:07,920
Jin, Tianna also studied in the US.

612
00:38:08,000 --> 00:38:10,920
- She's a consultant now.
- Okay, Mom.

613
00:38:12,040 --> 00:38:13,240
I know Mr. Shen.

614
00:38:13,840 --> 00:38:16,000
- He's a client of our company.
- Know each other?

615
00:38:16,520 --> 00:38:20,840
- They've known each other.
- So I'll go chat with him outside?

616
00:38:21,520 --> 00:38:22,760
- Sure.
- Great.

617
00:38:22,840 --> 00:38:23,960
Go chat with her.

618
00:38:25,000 --> 00:38:25,960
Go on.

619
00:38:29,840 --> 00:38:32,400
The other day, you were chasing Lin down
in the parking lot,

620
00:38:32,480 --> 00:38:34,280
and now you're out on a blind date.

621
00:38:34,360 --> 00:38:36,520
Mr. Shen, your time management
is really something.

622
00:38:38,320 --> 00:38:39,800
Fellow sufferers of the same fate.

623
00:38:39,880 --> 00:38:41,120
Cut each other some slack.

624
00:38:41,200 --> 00:38:42,960
Aren't you out on a blind date
behind your boyfriend's back?

625
00:38:45,360 --> 00:38:47,560
Don't talk nonsense.
I don't have a boyfriend.

626
00:38:49,120 --> 00:38:51,120
Okay, whatever you say.

627
00:38:52,800 --> 00:38:54,240
You're really…

628
00:38:54,960 --> 00:38:56,520
Why are you being so snarky?

629
00:38:57,720 --> 00:38:58,720
No wonder Lin doesn't like you.

630
00:39:03,960 --> 00:39:04,840
What, did I say something wrong?

631
00:39:07,680 --> 00:39:08,760
No. You're right.

632
00:39:09,960 --> 00:39:10,840
She really doesn't like me.

633
00:39:12,600 --> 00:39:14,320
By the way, how's she been?

634
00:39:16,080 --> 00:39:16,920
You wanna know?

635
00:39:18,600 --> 00:39:22,000
You think I'd be nice enough to tell you?

636
00:39:28,080 --> 00:39:29,200
Let's make a deal.

637
00:39:29,280 --> 00:39:31,520
Tell me how she's been,

638
00:39:32,040 --> 00:39:36,080
and I guarantee your mom won't bug you
for a long time.

639
00:39:39,080 --> 00:39:40,080
Really?

640
00:39:41,200 --> 00:39:42,960
- At least half a year?
- A whole year, even.

641
00:39:46,720 --> 00:39:48,400
What do you think they're talking about?

642
00:39:48,480 --> 00:39:50,320
They're really hitting it off.

643
00:39:51,360 --> 00:39:52,280
Now tell me.

644
00:39:52,800 --> 00:39:54,000
How's she been?

645
00:39:55,560 --> 00:39:57,000
She's fine. Everything's normal.

646
00:39:58,040 --> 00:39:59,720
- That's it?
- Yeah.

647
00:39:59,800 --> 00:40:00,880
That's worth a year?

648
00:40:00,960 --> 00:40:03,080
What else do you want?

649
00:40:03,160 --> 00:40:06,840
Lin got divorced
and ended up in the hospital.

650
00:40:06,920 --> 00:40:10,040
After all that, she comes back to work
as if nothing happened.

651
00:40:10,120 --> 00:40:12,760
You expect her to be heartbroken?

652
00:40:12,840 --> 00:40:14,160
Besides,

653
00:40:14,240 --> 00:40:17,840
you're the one pursuing her like crazy,
not the other way around.

654
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:19,000
Are you done?

655
00:40:19,520 --> 00:40:22,440
If you keep throwing out
these useless comments,

656
00:40:22,520 --> 00:40:23,440
I'm calling off the deal.

657
00:40:24,040 --> 00:40:25,360
No, then what…

658
00:40:26,200 --> 00:40:27,600
Then what else do you want to know?

659
00:40:28,600 --> 00:40:29,800
I want to know…

660
00:40:38,200 --> 00:40:39,720
I don't even know what I want to know.

661
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:46,520
I don't even know what she really wants.

662
00:40:49,160 --> 00:40:50,840
I told her to stop selling herself short,

663
00:40:51,760 --> 00:40:53,680
but she still told me to stay away.

664
00:40:53,760 --> 00:40:55,640
She said

665
00:40:55,720 --> 00:40:57,920
she wants to keep
her dignity and her pride.

666
00:41:01,200 --> 00:41:02,040
What are you laughing at?

667
00:41:03,760 --> 00:41:04,680
Sorry.

668
00:41:05,360 --> 00:41:07,240
I'm just laughing at how dumb you are.

669
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:09,160
What do you mean?

670
00:41:10,440 --> 00:41:13,560
What did she say she wanted to keep?

671
00:41:13,640 --> 00:41:14,840
Her dignity and pride.

672
00:41:14,920 --> 00:41:17,520
Then it must be because you did something

673
00:41:17,600 --> 00:41:19,120
that made her feel
like she lost her dignity.

674
00:41:19,200 --> 00:41:21,240
That's like dragging someone
who's scared of heights

675
00:41:21,320 --> 00:41:23,000
up to a rooftop and telling her,

676
00:41:23,080 --> 00:41:25,080
"Honey, don't be scared." Does that help?

677
00:41:29,640 --> 00:41:30,480
So that's it.

678
00:41:32,240 --> 00:41:34,080
Okay. Now you know. Go explain yourself.

679
00:41:36,400 --> 00:41:37,360
No rush.

680
00:41:38,520 --> 00:41:39,720
Never go into battle unprepared.

681
00:41:41,040 --> 00:41:42,280
Let me tell you something.

682
00:41:42,360 --> 00:41:45,840
Missy, don't think you can boss me around
on everything.

683
00:41:46,440 --> 00:41:48,240
If you were actually good
at this love stuff,

684
00:41:48,320 --> 00:41:49,960
you wouldn't be here tonight.

685
00:41:53,840 --> 00:41:55,080
I wasted my breath on you.

686
00:41:59,040 --> 00:42:00,240
It wasn't wasted.

687
00:42:01,320 --> 00:42:02,160
Come closer.

688
00:42:04,400 --> 00:42:05,480
I said come closer.

689
00:42:06,200 --> 00:42:07,680
Why should I come closer?

690
00:42:09,720 --> 00:42:10,920
The choice is yours.

691
00:42:19,760 --> 00:42:20,800
Is it okay now?

692
00:42:22,280 --> 00:42:24,520
- Take my arm.
- Take your arm?

693
00:42:37,520 --> 00:42:38,520
On my cue.

694
00:42:39,040 --> 00:42:42,280
I'll count to three,
and we turn around, look back,

695
00:42:42,360 --> 00:42:44,400
smile, and nod.

696
00:42:44,480 --> 00:42:45,320
Got it?

697
00:42:46,520 --> 00:42:48,240
I asked if you got it.

698
00:42:48,320 --> 00:42:49,160
Answer me properly.

699
00:42:51,520 --> 00:42:54,280
- Got it, Mr. Shen.
- Three, two, one.

700
00:43:00,520 --> 00:43:02,200
You two go ahead and chat.

701
00:43:02,280 --> 00:43:03,640
You two have a nice talk.

702
00:43:06,760 --> 00:43:11,120
But holding arms on a first blind date
is a bit much, isn't it?

703
00:43:11,200 --> 00:43:14,120
There's worse. Wanna try?

704
00:43:14,680 --> 00:43:16,400
- No thanks.
- So it wasn't wasted, was it?

705
00:43:17,560 --> 00:43:18,680
No, Mr. Shen.
